```

## 8. Tabs Component

**Use Tabs for view switching:**

```tsx
import { Tabs, TabsList, TabsTrigger, TabsContent } from '@/components/ui/tabs'

// ✅ CORRECT - Standard tabs
<Tabs defaultValue="all">
  <TabsList>
    <TabsTrigger value="all">All</TabsTrigger>
    <TabsTrigger value="active">Active</TabsTrigger>
    <TabsTrigger value="completed">Completed</TabsTrigger>
  </TabsList>
  <TabsContent value="all">
    <TaskList />
  </TabsContent>
</Tabs>
```

## 9. Skeleton Component

**Use Skeleton for loading states:**

```tsx
import { Skeleton } from '@/components/ui/skeleton'

// ✅ CORRECT - Loading skeleton
{isLoading ? (
  <div className="space-y-4">
    <Skeleton className="h-12 w-full" />
    <Skeleton className="h-12 w-full" />
    <Skeleton className="h-12 w-full" />
  </div>
) : (
  <TaskList tasks={tasks} />
)}

// ❌ WRONG - Don't create custom loading states
<div className="animate-pulse bg-slate-200 h-12" />  // Use Skeleton
```

## 10. Alert Component

**Use Alert for informational messages:**

```tsx
import { Alert, AlertTitle, AlertDescription } from '@/components/ui/alert'

// ✅ CORRECT - Semantic alerts
<Alert variant="destructive">
  <AlertCircle className="h-4 w-4" />
  <AlertTitle>Error</AlertTitle>
  <AlertDescription>
    Something went wrong. Please try again.
  </AlertDescription>
</Alert>

<Alert variant="default">
  <Info className="h-4 w-4" />
  <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
  <AlertDescription>
    This action cannot be undone.
  </AlertDescription>
</Alert>
```

## 11. Avatar Component (User Avatars)

**CRITICAL: Always use UserAvatar for internal users**

**DESIGN STANDARD: Avatars must be clean circles without borders or rings.** The bordered avatar style has been removed from the design system for visual consistency.

### Use UserAvatar for All Internal Users

```tsx
import { UserAvatar, UserAvatarStack } from '@/components/ui/user-avatar'

// ✅ CORRECT - Clean circle with role-based colors
<UserAvatar name="Jane Smith" role="Founder" size="md" />
<UserAvatar name="AI Assistant" role="AI_Agent" size="sm" />

// ❌ WRONG - Direct Avatar with manual colors
import { Avatar, AvatarFallback } from '@/components/ui/avatar'
<Avatar>
  <AvatarFallback className="bg-blue-100 text-blue-700">
    JS
  </AvatarFallback>
</Avatar>

// ❌ WRONG - Attempting to add borders (showBorder prop removed)
<UserAvatar name="John Doe" role="Executive" showBorder />  // Error: prop doesn't exist
```

### Role-Based Color System (Automatic)

UserAvatar automatically applies role-based colors using an **orange hierarchy**:
- **Founder** → Dark orange background (`bg-orange-100`)
- **Executive** → Light orange background (`bg-orange-50`)
- **Apprentice** → Neutral muted background (`bg-muted`)
- **AI_Agent** → Purple background with bot icon (`bg-purple-100`)
- **Default** → Neutral muted background

This creates clear visual hierarchy: Founders stand out most, Executives are visually secondary, Apprentices blend in.

### Size Variants

| Size | Use Case |
|------|----------|
| `xs` | Inline mentions, compact lists |
| `sm` | Dropdowns, messages |
| `md` | Default (cards, lists) |
| `lg` | Profile headers |
| `xl` | Large profile displays |
| `2xl` | Public profile view |
| `3xl` | Full profile pages |

### When to Use Direct Avatar

Only use `Avatar` (not `UserAvatar`) for:
- Non-user entities (organization logos)
- External users without roles (suppliers, buyers)
- Placeholder/decorative avatars

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - External user without role
<Avatar>
  <AvatarImage src={supplier.logo} />
  <AvatarFallback>SP</AvatarFallback>
</Avatar>
```

### Avatar Stacks (Multiple Users)

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Stack with overflow indicator (no borders needed)
<UserAvatarStack 
  users={assignees.map(a => ({
    id: a.id,
    name: a.full_name,
    role: a.role,
    avatarUrl: a.avatar_url
  }))}
  size="sm"
  max={4}
/>

// ❌ WRONG - Manual stack implementation
<div className="flex -space-x-2">
  {assignees.map(a => <Avatar key={a.id}>...</Avatar>)}
</div>
```

**Note:** Stacked avatars use `-space-x-2` for overlap and work perfectly without borders. The clean circle design maintains clarity even when overlapping.

### Common Violations

During codebase standardization, we found these anti-patterns:

1. **Direct Avatar with `bg-muted`** - Found in 8 files
2. **Custom InitialsAvatar components** - Found in timeline components
3. **Hardcoded `bg-foundry-*` colors** - Found in task feed
4. **Missing `role` field in queries** - Found in messaging
5. **Duplicate `getInitials` functions** - Found in 6 files
6. **Custom avatar stacks** - Found in Gantt view

See `.cursor/rules/avatar-standard.mdc` for complete anti-pattern documentation.

## Component Naming Convention

When creating custom components that wrap or extend base components:

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Descriptive, purpose-based names
TaskStatusBadge.tsx  // Specific to task statuses
OrderCard.tsx        // Specific to orders
CreateTaskDialog.tsx // Specific action + component type

// ❌ WRONG - Generic or unclear names
MyBadge.tsx          // Too vague
CustomCard.tsx       // Doesn't describe purpose
Dialog2.tsx          // Version numbers indicate poor planning
```

## Quick Checklist

Before committing any component usage:

- [ ] Badges use semantic variants (not custom colors)
- [ ] StatusBadge used for all status indicators
- [ ] **User avatars use UserAvatar component (not direct Avatar)**
- [ ] **Avatars are clean circles without borders or rings** - no `showBorder` prop
- [ ] **No hardcoded avatar backgrounds (bg-muted, bg-slate-*, bg-foundry-*)**
- [ ] **Database queries include `role` field for avatar coloring**
- [ ] Buttons use semantic variants and include loading states
- [ ] Icon-only buttons have `aria-label`
- [ ] Cards use Card component (not custom divs)
- [ ] Card padding not overridden
- [ ] Dialogs use `size` prop (not custom widths)
- [ ] Dialog footers: Cancel left, Submit right
- [ ] EmptyState used for zero-data views
- [ ] Skeleton used for loading states
- [ ] **CRITICAL: NO Sheet/side panels** - ONLY use Dialog
- [ ] **Z-index NOT overridden on UI primitives** (see `z-index-hierarchy.mdc`)
- [ ] **No `!bg-white`** - use `bg-background` instead
- [ ] **Run `./scripts/check-design-tokens.sh`** before committing

## Z-Index Rules

**CRITICAL:** Never override z-index on these components:

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - Breaks z-index hierarchy
<PopoverContent className="z-50">
<SelectContent className="z-50">
<DropdownMenuContent className="z-50">

// ✅ CORRECT - Let components manage their own z-index
<PopoverContent>
<SelectContent>
<DropdownMenuContent>
```

See `.cursor/rules/z-index-hierarchy.mdc` for the full z-index scale.
